PTX splitk-multi-peer-red
"Stream-K with several peers: each peer CTA adds its partial into the global workspace with a relaxed red, then fence.acq_rel.gpu and a relaxed red on the flag; the final CTA spins with ld.acquire.gpu until the flag counts both peers, then reads the workspace (CUTLASS sm90_tile_scheduler_stream_k.hpp:524-541, block_striped.h:221-223, barrier.h:116-124, 183-193). The acquire reads the second red of an RMW chain on the flag and must see both partials. Expected: forbidden."
{
w=0;
l=0;
P2:r0=0;
P2:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0        | P1@cta 1,cluster 0,gpu 0        | P2@cta 2,cluster 0,gpu 0 ;
 red.relaxed.gpu.global.add w, 1 | red.relaxed.gpu.global.add w, 1 | ld.acquire.gpu r0, l     ;
 fence.acq_rel.gpu               | fence.acq_rel.gpu               | ld.weak.global r1, w     ;
 red.relaxed.gpu.global.add l, 1 | red.relaxed.gpu.global.add l, 1 |                          ;
exists
(P2:r0 == 2 /\ P2:r1 != 2)
